{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoGCqnxfzWFtQRTuDYhW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't run the command yet. The `careful` skill requires your approval of this exact command first.\n\n**Command:**\n```\nbq rm -r -f -d example-project-dev:staging_old\n```\n\n**What it destroys:**\n- It deletes the dataset `staging_old` in project `example-project-dev`.\n- `-r` also deletes every table, view, and routine inside it.\n- `-f` skips bq's own confirmation prompt, so nothing will ask again.\n\n**Can it be undone?**\n- Not by anything I'd run. BigQuery has no undelete for a dataset.\n- Dataset time travel may let you recover deleted tables for a limited window, but that depends on the dataset's configured time-travel window (2 to 7 days). It is not a guaranteed rollback.\n- Nothing in this session has checked whether the dataset has a backup or snapshot.\n\nI haven't listed the dataset's contents, so I can't tell you how many tables it holds or whether anything still reads from it. I can run `bq ls` on it first if you want to check.\n\nReply \"yes\" to run the command exactly as written, or tell me to inspect the dataset first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":884,"cache_read_input_tokens":19615,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":884},"output_tokens":370,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa588247-7354-4857-9af6-c678a1ea4a15","uuid":"3f0cb2db-f167-484f-9c7c-601489420999","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:36:39.328Z","request_id":"req_011CgoGCqZZwCeYhq3n2NStu"}
